cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Swage in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Swage: turning variable-sized dense segments into efficient GPU tile tasks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Abhik
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhiksark/swage"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Swage is an experimental Python-embedded GPU compiler built on MLIR and
  LLVM. Programmers define segment-local computations in a Triton-like
  Python DSL; Swage lowers those semantics into cost-aware fixed-tile task
  graphs and generates NVIDIA GPU code through MLIR, LLVM, and NVPTX.
